\tag{fdip}
\title{Transport of rotation degrees and volume signs}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{A [translation block](fdip-016C) is labeled by its shift
multipliers. Within it a rotation can have several eigenvalues.
If two blocks are related by a symmetry, comparing those
eigenvalues requires a choice of rotation in each block.
Which changes come from the choices, and which come from the
action of the symmetry on complex scalars?}

\p{On an axis of the momentum grid the Hermitian symbol contains
just one direction operator. When does its eigenvalue determine
a transverse rotation degree after a volume sign is specified?}

\p{With the same Clifford directions and spin-fiber, carrying an axial representative #{0<|r_c|<N_c/2} through refinement preserves its transverse-product eigenvalue on the same joint spin eigenvector (\ref{fdip-01BS}).}

